NAME

ulibLocalTime - Returns current time


SYNOPSIS

void ulibLocalTime(time_t *tp, struct timeval *ReturnTM)
                        a0                a1


DESCRIPTION

This is a re-entrant library version of the standard C localtime()
function.  Note, however, that the parameters are different, since this
routine does not use non-re-entrant static variables.

This routine is used internally by ulibStoreTodaysDate(), and will probably
not be of much use to door programmers.

The ulibStoreTodaysDate() function is of much more importance.


